    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-sample/q5",
      "question": "<p>A pond initially contains 1000 litres of unpolluted water.</p><p>The pond is leaking at a constant rate of 20 litres per day.</p><p>It is suspected that contaminated water flows into the pond at a constant rate of 25 litres per day and that the contaminated water contains 2 grams of pollutant in every litre of water.</p><p>It is assumed that the pollutant instantly dissolves throughout the pond upon entry.</p><p>Given that there are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> grams of the pollutant in the pond after <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> days,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>show that the situation can be modelled by the differential equation,<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt}=50-\\frac{4x}{200+t}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Hence find the number of grams of pollutant in the pond after 8 days. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li>Explain how the model could be refined. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
        "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9fm0-01-sample/q05-ms-p06-1.svg\" alt=\"Official mark scheme for original question 5; source page 6, segment 1 of 2. Includes the original working, marks, alternative methods and examiner guidance in source order.\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:100%\"></figure>",
