      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-sample/q7",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:30mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9fm0-01-sample/q07-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2: a teardrop-shaped pendant of height 2 cm, shaded, with a vertical double-headed arrow marking the 2 cm height\"></figure><p>Figure 2 shows the image of a gold pendant which has height 2 cm. The pendant is modelled by a solid of revolution of a curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis. The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has parametric equations</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=\\cos\\theta+\\frac12\\sin2\\theta,\\qquad y=-(1+\\sin\\theta)\\qquad 0\\leqslant\\theta\\leqslant2\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that a Cartesian equation of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> is<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x^2=-(y^4+2y^3)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Hence, using the model, find, in cm³, the volume of the pendant. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
