    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-01-sample/q9",
      "question": "<p>A company plans to build a new fairground ride. The ride will consist of a capsule that will hold the passengers and the capsule will be attached to a tall tower. The capsule is to be released from rest from a point half way up the tower and then made to oscillate in a vertical line.</p><p>The vertical displacement, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> metres, of the top of the capsule below its initial position at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> seconds is modelled by the differential equation,</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"m\\frac{\\mathrm d^2x}{\\mathrm dt^2}+4\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt}+x=200\\cos t,\\qquad t\\geqslant0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\"></span> is the mass of the capsule including its passengers, in thousands of kilograms.</p><p>The maximum permissible weight for the capsule, including its passengers, is 30 000 N.</p><p>Taking the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g\"></span> to be <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}\"></span> and assuming the capsule is at its maximum permissible weight,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>explain why the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\"></span> is 3</li><li>show that a particular solution to the differential equation is<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=40\\sin t-20\\cos t\" data-display=\"true\"></div></li><li>hence find the general solution of the differential equation.</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(8)</span></li><li>Using the model, find, to the nearest metre, the vertical distance of the top of the capsule from its initial position, 9 seconds after it is released. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
        "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9fm0-01-sample/q09-ms-p10-1.svg\" alt=\"Official mark scheme for original question 9; source page 10, segment 1 of 2. Includes the original working, marks, alternative methods and examiner guidance in source order.\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:100%\"></figure>",
